Package: mint-arm-system
Version: 22.3.8
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Linux Mint ARM local build <mint-arm@localhost>
Depends: systemd-zram-generator, mint-arm-vm | mint-arm-pi
Conflicts: ubiquity-frontend-kde, oem-config-kde
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Description: Linux Mint ARM64 system settings
 Configuration for the unofficial arm64 build of Linux Mint 22.3, which runs on the Raspberry
 Pi and in virtual machines (mint-arm-pi and mint-arm-vm hold what only one of them needs):
  - on the first start, the system removes what its machine does not use: the Raspberry
    Pi's kernel, firmware and boot tools in a virtual machine, the virtual machine's kernel,
    GRUB and guest tools on a Raspberry Pi
  - compressed RAM swap (zram) and matching memory settings
  - a smaller systemd journal
  - Ubuntu's generic kernel installs without the device trees of physical boards, which no
    virtual machine uses (about 100 MB less); the Raspberry Pi kernel keeps its own
  - Firefox from Mozilla's arm64 apt repository, with Linux Mint's Firefox defaults
  - Ubuntu's snap-only Firefox, Thunderbird and Chromium packages are hidden, as
    Linux Mint hides snapd
  - Update Manager does not suggest Linux Mint mirrors, which carry no arm64 packages
  - the first-start setup gets Ubiquity's GTK front end back, never the KDE one, which
    apt would otherwise pick (with some 120 Qt and KDE packages)
